WEBVTT

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:19.990
<b>What's Wrong, Touko-senpai?</b>

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.490
<b>Ori Aca Festival</b>

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.240
Hime-chan!

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.620
Are you going to the club without me?

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.650
I am. I already finished the
 food staff's sanitary training.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.270
Why does the costume staff 
have to have a meeting now...

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.180
I do like this feeling of 
restlessness everywhere,

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.410
it's quite different than normal.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.880
I know, right?!

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.710
Just two more weeks and then 
it's time for the real thing!

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.260
The whole school is going to 
be one box of excitement!

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.690
I disagree to disagree to agree with that.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.280
Nao-chan?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.740
What's with that kimono?

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.560
It's a potential costume for the 
haunted mansion pork broth...

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.910
Did you say haunted mansion pork broth?

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.280
That sounds great!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.370
Is the pottery club doing something, too?

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.600
I guess we'll display the pieces
 we've made and try to sell them.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.390
Touko-senpai is really getting into it.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.590
She's trying to make a huge plate that will 
surpass the one she made for the contest!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.880
But this morning...

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.800
she looked kind of sad.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.030
Huh?

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.570
Touko-senpai?

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.890
Good morning!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.840
Touko-senpai?

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.160
Oh! Good morning.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.280
Huh?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.290
<b>Pottery Club</b>

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.310
Touko-senpai?

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.690
I wonder what's wrong.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.880
<b>Pottery Club</b>

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:03.870
Touko-senpai!

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.840
Toyokawa-san...

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.870
Senpai?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.670
Did you forget something 
back in the class room?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.420
No...

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.570
I don't think I can do it today.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.550
Approaching your work in a bad mood
 is rude to the pottery.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:36.840
Um...

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.770
So, there's this gohei mochi 
place I found online.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.580
Want to go check it out?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.600
<b><i>Kisouma</i></b>

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.600
Gohei Mochi

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.760
I can't believe this is their last one!

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.500
This place usually runs out of their 
gohei mochi and ohagi before noon.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.410
Touko-senpai, please have it!

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.120
It's fine! I've been eating
 these since I was little.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.600
Well, thank you, then.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.460
That's so good!

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.700
I'm glad.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:20.550
But I was trying to cheer you up.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.210
Oh!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.500
Don't worry. They also make delicious takoyaki.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.630
It's hot. You're righ! Theef aa rea' good!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.270
Wight?

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.880
Touko-senpai, you said "Wight!"

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.800
Was it that funny?

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.900
I'm sorry.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.860
Oh, no, please let me—

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.540
I can't believe I let this 
silly thing get to me.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:58.560
Huh?

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.430
I should be so used to it, 
but it got me so depressed.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.940
Yesterday, I went to my grandfather's 
studio to take him his dinner.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.240
Can I come in, grandfather?

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:30.180
I've told you to leave the food by the door.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.420
I'm sorry...

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.780
Just one thing...

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:39.960
I'm going to exhibit again at
 this year's cultural festival!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.480
I plan on further developing the 
piece I made for the contest.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.870
So I was hoping you could come see it.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.680
Well, if I can make it.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.820
He's said "If I can make it" five times now.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.640
He's never shown up though.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.920
I act all serious,

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.490
but I'm actually a liar.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.410
What do you mean?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.470
I even chided Mika-chan 
about this, back then.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:29.850
The Mino ware contest is here 
at last and it sure would be

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:32.950
nice if all three of us 
won some sort of award.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.640
Right, Touko-senpai?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.930
It's not like I made it for an award.

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.600
I remember you saying that.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.190
It sounds like something you would say.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.830
But the truth is, I wanted to 
win that Best in Show prize.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.210
But anyone would want to win that.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.890
That was the only reason I made my piece.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.290
Maybe that's why I didn't win.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.390
It was so much fun when 
I was in kindergarten.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.610
I got praised, no matter what I made.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.240
Now that he knows what I can do,

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.580
maybe he's become bored with me.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.600
Well, I don't think that's it.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.660
Huh?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.390
Now that Aoki-san's skills are higher,

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:27.340
her grandfather's criteria for 
giving praise is higher, too.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.600
Huh...

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:31.840
There was a super elite baseball player 
who went on to become a commentator.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:36.120
He generated a lot of buzz because 
he wouldn't praise the players.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.370
But why not?

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.330
It's a way of acknowledging 
someone's professional status.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.620
He said that excellent plays 
are expected if you're a pro.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.620
In the end, it became a bit of a joke.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:51.910
No matter how good a play someone made, 
he would just say, "That's ordinary."

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:55.480
I wonder what would make Senpai feel better.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.640
She just needs to cut loose 
and get out of that rut.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.380
Cut loose, huh?

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.470
Touko-senpai, please 
come to the outlet 
mall with me tomorrow~

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:26.460
Touko-senpai, please 
come to the outlet 
mall with me tomorrow~

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.460
Where did this come from?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.170
Touko-senpai, please 
come to the outlet 
mall with me tomorrow~ 

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.170
Where did this come from?

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.460
Touko-senpai, please 
come to the outlet 
mall with me tomorrow~ 

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.460
Where did this come from?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.590
Touko-senpai, please 
come to the outlet 
mall with me tomorrow~ 

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.590
Where did this come from?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.590
Then let's go.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.680
I just had the urge to cut loose. 

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.680
Where did this come from?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.680
Then let's go.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.720
I just had the urge to cut loose. 

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.720
Then let's go.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.860
<i>It worked!</i>

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.470
Thanks, Kukuri-chan!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.370
<i>No problem!</i>

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.890
It's been so long!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.640
We still ended up in a place like this.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.700
That's the saga of the pottery club.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:06.430
At first, I thought Ryota Aoki 
might be a relative of yours.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.330
That would've been nice.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:12.320
It does make me jealous, though.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:16.080
I would love to sell my stuff 
 in a store like this one day.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:20.160
This is that one piece I loved online!

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.250
It's even better in real life.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.770
Wow, it is really pretty.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.080
And will you be purchasing that?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.210
I couldn't.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:32.830
<b>Sun Ceramics Bowl 

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.170
Even at 40% off, it's this much.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.750
Ugh, six figures!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.260
Eek.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:35.850
Anyway, it doesn't really suit me.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.350
Thanks for the invitation today.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:46.450
I got some new clothes and 
it was all so much fun.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.320
That's great!

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.710
Right, Hime-chan?

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.730
Uh, yeah!

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.320
<i>But...</i>

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.230
Hime-chan?

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.490
Ximena-san?

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.110
¡Increíble!

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.290
It's been a while!

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.280
Oh, Touko-senpai, this is...

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.920
¡Encantada!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:17.930
Nice to meet you!

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.460
My name is Ximena Valdez!

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:22.140
My name is Aoki. I'm the 
president of the pottery club.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.020
President... of the pottery club?

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:27.470
That's right! She's the one 
who leads and teaches us!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.980
Wow, that's amazing!

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.340
No, I'm nothing special...

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.310
Then you can probably solve the mystery!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:35.960
Huh?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.620
So I found a really mysterious 
tool in the pottery studio.

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:42.510
It was kept far away from 
all the other tools,

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.280
which made it super-duper suspicious.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.540
Please solve the mystery, President-san!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.510
But I'm not—

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:51.130
All right! Our senpai 
will solve this mystery.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.070
What?!

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:54.770
¡Muchas gracias!

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:56.860
Could you bring it over here?

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:57.930
¡Sí!

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.800
But, Toyokawa-san...

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.960
Doesn't that sound interesting?

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.340
Why don't we just take a look at it?

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.270
Sure...

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:29.460
The bob-haired one and her friends try to solve 
the mystery that the Mexican girl brings them.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:35.310
<b>Mini Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:33.310
Whilst doing that, Forehead 
manages to open a new door!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.460
Next time, "The Pottery Club 
of Endless Mysteries!"

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>The Pottery Club of Endless Mysteries</b>

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:39.350
Don't turn back! Just keep running 
forward towards the future!
